    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Solve the equation $\\dfrac{1}{x}+\\dfrac{1}{2x}+\\dfrac{3}{4x}+\\dfrac{5}{12}=\\dfrac{7}{24}$ by first multiplying both sides of the equation by $24x$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=-18$",
      "worked": "Multiply both sides by $24x$ ($x\\ne0$).\n$$\\begin{align*}24x\\left(\\frac1x+\\frac1{2x}+\\frac3{4x}+\\frac5{12}\\right)&=24x\\left(\\frac7{24}\\right)\\\\24+12+18+10x&=7x\\\\54+10x&=7x\\\\54+3x&=0\\\\3x&=-54\\\\x&=-18\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
